	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Détermine la forme canonique du polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$.\n\n$P(x)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "h",
					"expression": "1..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "1..9;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "eval:-2*h"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "eval:h^2+k"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["c != 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "(x{{eval:-h;+}})^2{{eval:k;+}}",
					"requiredForm": {
						"pattern": "u*($x+v)^2+w"
					}
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"La forme canonique s'écrit $a(x-\\alpha)^2+\\beta$, avec $a={{a}}$, $\\alpha=\\dfrac{-b}{2a}$ et $\\beta=P(\\alpha)$.",
					"$$\\alpha=\\dfrac{-b}{2a}=\\dfrac{ {{eval:-b}} }{ {{eval:2*a}} }={{eval:-b/(2*a)}}$$",
					"$$\\begin{align}\\beta &= P\\left({{eval:-b/(2*a)}}\\right) \\\\ &= {{a}}\\times\\left({{eval:-b/(2*a)}}\\right)^2{{eval:b;+}}\\times\\left({{eval:-b/(2*a)}}\\right){{eval:c;+}} \\\\ &= {{eval:c-b^2/(4*a)}}\\end{align}$$",
					"Donc $P(x)=(x{{eval:-h;+}})^2{{eval:k;+}}$."
				]
			}
		},
